What we use from Slidev:

- The published npm package `@slidev/parser` (MIT) splits slides.md into slides and
  reads frontmatter and notes. It is a dependency, not copied code.
- The click logic in src/app/lib/clicks.ts, slide-ng-click.ts and slide-ng-clicks.ts is a port of
  Slidev's packages/client/composables/useClicks.ts and its v-click / v-after / v-clicks
  modules, rewritten for Angular.
- The layout names, structure and styles (src/app/layouts and src/styles/layouts.css, from Slidev's
  client layouts and default theme), the first-slide-is-cover rule, the 16:9 canvas scaling formula and the
  click CSS classes follow Slidev's design.
- The navigation bar, context menu, overview, goto box, keyboard shortcuts, table of contents, slide transitions
  and the small built-in components (src/app/ui, lib/shortcuts.ts, lib/toc-tree.ts, lib/transitions.ts, builtin/,
  lib/slide-ng-switch.ts, lib/slide-ng-click-gap.ts) are ports of the matching Slidev client code, rewritten for Angular.

- The styles in src/styles/code.css and src/styles/presenter.css, a few shortcut rules in uno.config.mjs, and the
  presenter page and drawing tools (src/app/presenter, src/app/drawing) follow Slidev's client code and are rewritten for Angular.
- The agent skill in skills/slide-ng follows the structure of Slidev's own agent skill: the topic table in SKILL.md, the
  category prefixes of the reference files (core-, diagram-, animation-, ...) and many of the file names. The text is
  our own and describes slide.ng; the structure and topic list are adapted from Slidev's skill (MIT).
- The official themes (seriph, shibainu, bricks, apple-basic) are not in this repository: they live in the slide.ng-themes repository,
  which carries their MIT attribution to the Slidev themes and says that no CC BY-NC-SA asset was copied. `theme: default` is the built-in look
  (see above).

